{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-27154-r4522780","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Grotten Hans (Steamed Sweet Bread)","sourcePageId":27154,"sourceRevision":"4522780","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-11T19:49:37Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Grotten%20Hans%20(Steamed%20Sweet%20Bread)&oldid=4522780","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:15.620Z","sourceCategories":["Category:German recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for pudding","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using lard","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Steamed recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"a59b20f556249385f15d5843479827e5db68b82af9c316d1801198502e08abc0","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Bread recipes|time=2 hours 30 minutes|difficulty=3}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Grotten hans''' is a recipe that has been called a big dumpling but is basically a steamed [[Cookbook:Pudding|pudding]]. The recipe was traditional in the German areas of Russia.<ref>[http://www.lib.ndsu.nodak.edu/grhc/archrecipes/index.cgi?cat=German-Russian NDSU Recipe Index]</ref>\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Batter ===\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Lard|lard]] or [[Cookbook:Corn Oil|oil]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:salt|salt]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n*2 tsp [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*½ cup white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:egg|eggs]], beaten\n*3 cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n\n=== Raisin sauce ===\n*2 cup [[Cookbook:raisin|raisins]]\n*2 cup [[Cookbook:water|water]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*1 scant tsp [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*½ cup white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cornstarch|Cornstarch]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# [[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] together lard, sugar and salt. Mix in eggs.\n# Combine flour and baking powder. Add this flour mixture to the lard mixture alternatively with the milk. Mix well.\n# Pour batter into a well-greased 2-pound coffee can or other heat-safe mold. A piece [[Cookbook:Parchment Paper|parchment paper]] on the bottom of the can works well to prevent sticking. Cover with [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]], and tie this on with a string.\n# Set this tin into a large pot of hot water a few inches (~3) deep. Let [[Cookbook:Steaming|steam]] for 2 hours.\n# Mix raisins, water, lemon juice, cinnamon and sugar in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]]. [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] for 1 hour. Mix in a bit or cornstarch, and cook until thickened.\n# Unmold the grotten hans, and serve with the sauce.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* The old way to cook this involved boiling in a cloth: Dip a towel in hot water, then cold water, then sprinkle with flour. Pour dumpling batter onto towel and tie up. Drop into [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiling]] water and cook for 2 hours.\n* Cherry sauce is nice also.\n\n==References==\n<references/>\n\n[[Category:German recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pudding]]\n[[Category:Steamed recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lard]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Grotten Hans (Steamed Sweet Bread)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"¼ cup lard or oil","sourceText":"¼ cup lard or oil","amountText":"¼ cup lard or oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tsp salt","sourceText":"1 tsp salt","amountText":"1 tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup milk","sourceText":"1 cup milk","amountText":"1 cup milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 tsp baking powder","sourceText":"2 tsp baking powder","amountText":"2 tsp baking powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"½ cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"½ cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"3 eggs, beaten","sourceText":"3 eggs, beaten","amountText":"3 eggs, beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"3 cup flour","sourceText":"3 cup flour","amountText":"3 cup flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 cup raisins","sourceText":"2 cup raisins","amountText":"2 cup raisins","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 cup water","sourceText":"2 cup water","amountText":"2 cup water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 tsp lemon juice","sourceText":"1 tsp lemon juice","amountText":"1 tsp lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"1 scant tsp cinnamon","sourceText":"1 scant tsp cinnamon","amountText":"1 scant tsp cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-12","name":"½ cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"½ cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"½ cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-13","name":"Cornstarch","sourceText":"Cornstarch","amountText":"Cornstarch","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Cream together lard, sugar and salt. Mix in eggs.","sourceText":"Cream together lard, sugar and salt. Mix in eggs.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Combine flour and baking powder. Add this flour mixture to the lard mixture alternatively with the milk. Mix well.","sourceText":"Combine flour and baking powder. Add this flour mixture to the lard mixture alternatively with the milk. Mix well.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Pour batter into a well-greased 2-pound coffee can or other heat-safe mold. A piece parchment paper on the bottom of the can works well to prevent sticking. Cover with foil, and tie this on with a string.","sourceText":"Pour batter into a well-greased 2-pound coffee can or other heat-safe mold. A piece parchment paper on the bottom of the can works well to prevent sticking. Cover with foil, and tie this on with a string.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Set this tin into a large pot of hot water a few inches (~3) deep. Let steam for 2 hours.","sourceText":"Set this tin into a large pot of hot water a few inches (~3) deep. Let steam for 2 hours.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Mix raisins, water, lemon juice, cinnamon and sugar in a saucepan. Simmer for 1 hour. Mix in a bit or cornstarch, and cook until thickened.","sourceText":"Mix raisins, water, lemon juice, cinnamon and sugar in a saucepan. Simmer for 1 hour. Mix in a bit or cornstarch, and cook until thickened.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Unmold the grotten hans, and serve with the sauce.","sourceText":"Unmold the grotten hans, and serve with the sauce.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:27154","recordId":"wikibooks-27154-r4522780","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4522780","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Grotten%20Hans%20(Steamed%20Sweet%20Bread)&oldid=4522780","sourceSha256":"a59b20f556249385f15d5843479827e5db68b82af9c316d1801198502e08abc0","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"reviewStatus":"source-extracted-unreviewed","changeNotice":"Source-language section extraction; markup removed. Not culinarily reviewed, translated or runtime-approved.","recipe":{"name":"Grott